      "description": {
        "fun": "A tiny turtle whose shell only forms and hardens after it hatches, and whose grooved, rounded shape lets it swim at high speed. It sprays foamy water from its mouth with great accuracy. Its English name mixes 'squirt' and 'turtle', a nod to the water guns kids loved, while its Japanese name, Zenigame, says its shell looks like an old coin.",
        "guide": "A small, light-blue turtle Pokémon whose shell forms and hardens after birth. It withdraws into its shell for protection, swims fast thanks to the shell's streamlined shape and sprays water accurately from its mouth. It is one of the first partner Pokémon of Kanto and evolves into Wartortle.",
        "tagline": "A pocket-sized turtle with a built-in water gun",
